{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Aaron lifted his hands toward the people.</b> Toward them, and our predecessors derived from here the form of the priestly blessing." "<b>And he came down.</b> As I have shown you, there are many, and he had already come down from offering the people's sin offering and their burnt offering and the peace offerings." "The sense of <b>and he came down</b> is on account of the altar, whose height was three cubits. Afterward Moses and Aaron came into the Tent of Meeting, and perhaps they came to pray concerning the fire, that it should go forth, and when they came out they both blessed the people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:14.509556364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}